{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456130-combination-discipline-question","id":1456130,"title":"Combination Discipline question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-04T09:26:12-07:00","id":1456130,"title":"Combination Discipline question","content":"It's been awhile since I have been asked but can a Combination Discipline be created from two variations of the same Discipline? Specifically, the player wants to combine Protean 1 and 5 to be able to see in darkness while in mist form. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24119-alucardtes","name":"Alucardtes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24119_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-04T09:33:36-07:00","id":1456131,"title":"","content":"Why does that even need a combo discipline?<br /> <br /> Just activate the first one.<br /> <br /> then activate the second one.<br /> <br /> There's nothing anywhere stating that effects like that don't stack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-04T10:16:18-07:00","id":1456136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alucardtes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456130-combination-discipline-question#post1456130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been awhile since I have been asked but can a Combination Discipline be created from two variations of the same Discipline? Specifically, the player wants to combine Protean 1 and 5 to be able to see in darkness while in mist form. Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be a Power mixing capabilities from the same Discipline, so it would not be a Combination Discipline Power. I see nothing against the possibility of developing such Powers,<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456130-combination-discipline-question?p=1456131#post1456131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does that even need a combo discipline?<br /> <br /> Just activate the first one.<br /> <br /> then activate the second one.<br /> <br /> There's nothing anywhere stating that effects like that don't stack.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that Mist Form should come with seeing in the dark by default. After all, the Vampire in Mist Form switches to a kind of extrasensory perception of her or his surroundings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Di